  "id": "spine",
  "term": "spine",
  "definition": "In this context, a spine means a dendritic spine: a small structural feature on neurons that helps prefrontal brain circuits combine incoming information. Loss of these spines in the prefrontal cortex is described as a shared brain abnormality in several neuropsychiatric disorders and may contribute to problems with cognition such as attention, working memory, and decision-making.",
